Subject: LLVM IR dual DataLayout, relaxed RAUW type assert, and non-integral pointer analysis guards
Upstream-Base: llvmorg-20.1.8 (87f0227cb60147a26a1eeb4fb06e3b505e9c7261)
Fil-C-Head: cede3de02b42b58a14acc9ce39c9894ab952a915 (branch deluge)

Adds Module::DLAfterFilC and AsmParser/AsmWriter support for pre-/post-Fil-C
DataLayouts, relaxes Value::doRAUW type-equality assertions required during
in-place Fil-C IR lowering, and guards IR/Analysis folds against invalid
transformations on non-integral pointers.

Fil-C-Origin-Commits (4):
  bd283c36d1aea6e74c16287f065bb76aee6fb1b7 2026-07-15 Fix #263. Also add some scripts to simplify incrementally testing clang changes on /opt/fil.
  b7dd5927a78f42563e0b1dd97aa07be31903afd8 2026-05-14 Enable direct function calls to skip the global getter call and function capability checks in the common case using ELF weak symbol tricks. This is a >1% speed-up on PizBench9019.
  d950cf057e4764ec3605b75ad8855e054c55c233 2025-09-14 Fixed a bunch of cases of obvious UB causing LLVM to optimize an operation that should have panicked into some kind of no-op. Resolves issue #56.
  d292f5dbb951d549fc9b053950d5a330d532b361 2025-08-22 Rebase Fil-C to clang/llvm 20.1.8

